{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 01:45 +07\n# Task: slice 7e, documentation for phase 7 (codex writes; a non-codex reviewer checks it against the code)\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e`, branch `srvm-phase7e` from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b, 7c merged; 7d is in review on branch srvm-phase7d, its facts are in `collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.report.md`). DOCS ONLY: edit nothing under `src/` or `test/`. Edit ONLY: `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `docs/orchestrator-log.md` is NOT yours (the other orchestrator owns it; put your log text in your report instead), and your report `collab/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3: cursor (immutable dao.stream value), cursor cell (the carrier's box, `:yin.k/cc-<n>`), cursor-ref (the sealed ref a program holds), cell (the heap box only). Read: `collab/phase7-plan.md` (3.1-3.9 and the slice sections), `collab/7a-report.md` (D3 doc amendment list and codex 7a review `collab/7a-review.md` if present), the 7b and 7c reports, `collab/7c-review.md`, the 7d report, and READ THE CODE so every sentence is true: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{rows,rows/checkpoint,handoff,holder/export,holder/driver,compose}.cljc`. Owner rulings that bind the text: fork custody slot is nil; REPL custody gap accepted until phase 8; install checks (link-id = parent, image address = manifest) are enforced at lower; code and trees load through the linker's source-index, fetch and admission; A is the only code identity; the AST is never lost; BLAKE3; no compat or version dispatch (the old codec versions 0/1/2 remain only until phase 8); lease, epoch and holder never enter a body; the de Bruijn kernels are BACKENDS of the semantic-register VM with a documented fragment, kept after phase 8, not widened.\nWrite, marking each amended clause \"**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)**\" with a one-line reason:\n(1) continuation design: sections 2.5 and 2.6 (custody slot by kind: fork nil in every row, exclusive roots carry policy/occurrence/arbitration/next-op-seq/origin, halted exclusive carry origin only; five keys only), 7.1 and 7.2 (the lift `:header`, the lower stages stores, pendings and install records, dependencies, custody once for the tree, then attach; `:fenced` mode; pack vs root id; sorted rows), 8.4 (phase 7's entry conditions met), a new 10.8 inventory of phase 7's amendments in the 10.6/10.7 style, 11 (close 6b Q3 and Q4 as implemented or as stated by the code; leave others open; record the 7a D2 ruling: root is in the baseline, so a re-emitted id-counter variant is `:variant-conflict` and the only equal-baseline encoding is the same root in another row order);\n(2) transport tuples draft: 5.5 custody table (fork = nil in every row; the slot admits only the five custody keys), 7 (pack address vs root id; rows sorted by id in `emit`), 9 (the fenced lower), 5.4 install verification as implemented;\n(3) UCF: 7.7.4 (the export-recovery object is now format 2: pack address, root, base64 pack, local header, `:yin.k/state` with gate/origins/issued/issues/children; no second snapshot body), 7.11.1 clauses 1-5 and 10 (stage letters and the inspector citation `yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint`), AND the three owner-approved 7.11 edits (about lines 2886-2897 and 3050-3062 of the UCF file): say the stack and register kernels are backends checked on their documented fragment and refuse the rest before attach; replace \"the three engines intended to reconstruct canonical frames\" by \"the canonical kernel and its two backends\"; add a pointer to continuation design 4.6.\nDo not invent: if the code does something the plan did not say, state what the code does and list the discrepancy under \"design defects\" in the report. Foreground only. Report: 15-line plain summary, edits by file and section, discrepancies between the plan and the code, open questions, the orchestrator-log text (10 lines) for the owner to paste. End READY.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
